 "text": "Sound: a stripped-down, hypnotic techno loop: kick on every beat, off-beat hats and a clicky rim shot in a skipping sixteenth pattern. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 128. Kick on every BEAT. Hats from a Sequencer on the off-beats. The rim: a high, very short triangle blip, from a Sequencer on sixteenths (its 8 steps cover half a bar, so the pattern plays twice). A short Delay on the mix makes the rim skip.\n\nTweak: the rim's steps, the delay's TIME and FEEDBACK, TEMPO.",
